  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a complex but interconnected pathway where (2S,3S,4R)-10-De-O-Carbamoyl-12-O-Carbamoyl Streptothricin E acts as a target for several compounds that ultimately target Glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate dehydrogenase. This compound is linked to PITSLRE serine/threonine-protein kinase CDC2L2, which is a target of multiple agents, including 7-Chloro-indole-1-acetic acid, Phlegmanol C, and Gingkolic Acid. These compounds, in turn, all share a common effect on Glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate dehydrogenase, indicating a potential mechanism of action through the modulation of CDC2L2. The evidence suggests that the target enzyme Glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate dehydrogenase is involved in a metabolic pathway that is influenced by these compounds, possibly through the activation or inhibition of CDC2L2. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role for the target enzyme in cellular processes that are modulated by the drug, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
